# A glass set by name (cmdref: MODify; Prescription I/O) on the manual's ImageDemo.in: MOD GlassElt(6)=BK7 puts the
# catalog's Sellmeier coefficients on the first relay surface, the trace uses the glass index (the OPD moves), SAVE writes
# GlassType= Sellmeier, and the saved deck reloads and traces to the same OPD.  Before, the NEW dialog's and MOD's
# glass branches copied the coefficients but left GlassType at 0 = Hartmann (MOD also left LGlass false): SAVE
# wrote 'GlassType= Hartmann', the reader refused it ('** Unknown glass type at Elt 6') and the trace through
# the lens lost every ray (macos-fd 2026-10-19, Section 4's Refractors tutorial; PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 1.2 (rr)).
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/ImageDemo.in
cd $TMP
old ImageDemo.in
opd 13
/null
mod
GlassElt(6)=BK7
q
opd 13
/null
save bk7
old bk7.in
opd 13
/null
! grep -c 'GlassType=  Sellmeier' bk7.in
# EXPECT: GlassElt\(\s*6\) = BK7
# The deck's IndRef 1.61783 gives 3.6057e-4 at the image; BK7's Sellmeier index at 0.7 um gives 4.0064e-4, and the
# reloaded deck gives the same 4.0064e-4 (5 figures, rule 2).
# EXPECT: RMS OPD error is\s+3\.605\d*D-04[\s\S]*?GlassElt\(\s*6\) = BK7[\s\S]*?RMS OPD error is\s+4\.006\d*D-04
# EXPECT: Input file \S*bk7\.in\s+being loaded[\s\S]*?RMS OPD error is\s+4\.006\d*D-04
# EXPECT: ^1\s*$
# EXPECT-NOT: Unknown glass type
# EXPECT-NOT: All rays are obscured or lost
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
